    {
      "title": "Harmanpreet, Deepti lead India to ODI series win against Zimbabwe",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/harmanpreet-deepti-lead-india-to-odi-series-win-against-zimbabwe-126102500700_1.html",
      "description": "Harmanpreet Kaur was brutal and Deepti Sharma sublime as their twin centuries headlined India's commanding 121-run victory over minnows Zimbabwe in the second women's ODI here on Sunday.\nIndia thus took an unassailable 2-0 lead in the three-match series having won the first match by a comfortable nine-wicket margin.\nHaving posted a formidable 328 for 6, the home team's spinners, led by left-arm orthodox bowler Vaishnavi Sharma (four wickets), bowled Zimbabwe out for a paltry 207 in 48.5 overs. After scoring her century, Deepti polished off the opposition tail with figures of 3 for 32.\nHarmanpreet, whose second coming as a pure batter has been nothing short of breathtaking, struck 126 off 121 balls laced with 15 well-timed boundaries. This was Harmanpreet's eighth WODI century after she hit a match-winning 91 in one of the WT20Is played earlier.\nShe had an able companion in Deepti, who remained unbeaten on 106 off 86 balls with 15 hits to the fence.\nHarmanpreet regaled a sizable cr",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-26T04:19:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cricket remains my happiness: Harmanpreet opens up on life beyond captaincy",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/cricket-remains-my-happiness-harmanpreet-opens-up-on-life-beyond-captaincy-126102500745_1.html",
      "description": "Veteran batter Harmanpreet Kaur has come to terms with life beyond captaincy and said she wants to keep enjoying her batting after producing yet another superlative knock in India's 121-run win over Zimbabwe in the second ODI.\nAfter scoring a fine 91 in a T20 International against Zimbabwe few days back, Harmanpreet struck her eighth ODI hundred in India's series-clinching victory against same opposition, underlining her enduring value to the team with the bat.\n\"I am someone who likes to live life close to reality. This is the reality now, and I want to accept it,\" Harmanpreet said at post match presentation ceremony.\n\"Cricket is something that gives me happiness and batting is something I have enjoyed throughout my career. Just want to enjoy batting.\"\nHarmanpreet added that captaincy was not on her mind when she was in the middle, as her priority was to take responsibility and bat according to the situation.\n\"When you are batting, you don't think about these things. You are batti",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-26T04:15:18"
    }
